t(27, 215, """Whole groups of people, not one particular person, are pained by this picture, as if a forefinger had been raised in the face of a qarin and it hissed and seethed at it .. They say: We were told: “Your fathers went astray before, and you went astray with them” .. So they said: “Our misguidance is dearer to us than what you call us to .. Misguidance settled so firmly in our hearts that we imagined it to be Qur'an, the light of prophethood and a path of guidance with no doubt in it .. The road has taken us far from the road .. We were part of everyone when they went astray, and we are no exception .. But when we accused everyone of misguidance, we forgot that we are of …""")

t(27, 1500, """Do not take a fatwa on personal-status matters from a scholar under sixty, for I see muftis in their twenties, thirties and forties giving people fatwas that are lame, or lame and reckless, that neither sustain a life nor straighten a crookedness. A fatwa on personal status never rests only on memorising the Noble Qur'an and the hadiths with sound chains, because personal status requires life wisdom and life experience. Whoever follows muftis under 60 sees a crookedness in …""")

t(27, 1870, """What makes the letter ẓāʼ (ظ) a ḍād (ض) among some peoples? So that one of them says “ḍahr” instead of “ẓahr”? When will our tampering with the Arabic language, the language of the Qur'an, stop?!""")

h(27, 2250, """My beautiful language""")

t(29, 740, """Breaking the laws of physics is real, but beware of misunderstanding it, for in that lies ruin

A small number of the brothers who write to me privately and a few of the commenters have, over the past months — some of them raising questions about feats that break physics — asked me to talk about matters I do not much like to go into, because whoever has not experienced it will not grasp it .. his mind will not bear it .. Feats that break physics, though they are an existing reality in which we believe with complete faith, definitely, decisively and without a second word do not belong to the grave-worshippers. Rather, everyone who worships a grave and the one in the grave is a dajjal for whom nothing of the law of physics is broken; he only babbles to people, play-acts, lies and deceives.

Even so, I will speak about feats that break physics for a very important purpose, the most important purpose of all in my view .. The purpose is that we believe and are certain that Allah Most High has power over all things with the certainty of an eyewitness who sees with his heart and his eye, not the certainty of a mind built on transmitted text alone. Rather, the transmitted text (the Book of Allah Most High) takes hold of the heart and the eye as a vision, a witnessing of fact and reality. And although ((most)) people know this orally and by reciting the Book of Allah, many souls turn away from being certain of it in heart, soul and spirit, or have no desire for it, or find it too hard!

As for breaking the laws and breaking physics, it is established by an explicit text in the Book of our Lord the Almighty for humans and not for jinn, in the story of Asif ibn Barkhiya, may Allah be pleased with him, the companion and associate of Allah's prophet Solomon, peace be upon him, when he brought to Allah's prophet""")

t(29, 1310, """Solomon the throne of Bilqis, the very throne itself and not a copy or an image of it .. He brought it to him without moving from his place, that is, Asif .. He brought a perceptible body made of wood and many other materials, tangible and perceptible, which the hand can touch, hold and feel .. He brought it from Yemen to Palestine in a fraction of a second or the blink of an eye, so the queen's palace in Yemen was truly emptied of the throne and its place became vacant.

As for the one who did that, he was a righteous man of the sons of Adam, peace be upon him, not a jinni, nor a marid, nor an ifrit. Therefore the breaking of the law is established and confirmed by the text of the Book of Allah the Almighty, our Lord, the All-Powerful, the Giver, the Subduer (He subdues physics and the laws of the universe).

The problem is not in all of us believing in this truth with complete faith. The problem is the dajjals' use of this faith and this knowledge of faith among a number of Muslims in order to pretend that they do the like of what Asif ibn Barkhiya did. This is unacceptable and cannot be accepted or believed, because it holds a great trial for people and draws the hearts of the ignorant among them into corruption, so that they think the wali is a prophet and a messenger; indeed some of them have worshipped the awliya, prostrated to them and prostrated to their graves, with no karamat at all, only lies and deception. So what then if the true awliya, who are real on earth and no lie, were to announce themselves .. What if they announced their karamat, which need not be of the kind that moves matter from place to place.

As for the one who asks me whether there can be, in the creation of Allah the Almighty and among His servants, in our time or in any time, someone who transports matter as Asif ibn Barkhiya did, or even transports himself, I say: definitely possible, very possible, and I find no problem in that, on a fixed rule that does not change: Allah has power over all things. But I do not believe the words of any person who comes and tells me “I do such-and-such” of what breaks the physical nature of the earth's laws .. A claim like this does not concern me; I do not accept it and no one else accepts it. So our problem is with the claim, not with the truth and reality that the matter is very possible, and there is never any problem in its happening. For the transport of perceptible matter is established in the Book of our Lord, and just as our Lord is definitely and certainly able to enable a human to transport lifeless inanimate matter, so our Lord, the All-Powerful, the Almighty, is definitely and certainly able to enable any of His creatures to be transported in his own living matter.

As for me, I was asked and answered that nothing like transfer or transport has happened to me; rather I have witnessed other things and matters in which the laws were completely broken .. As for what relates to transfer, I once wished in my heart to see what transfer means and how it feels .. That was months ago, and I saw a dream in which I saw myself at a place on a highway and suddenly I was transferred into a city, and I felt the transfer in the dream .. The transfer of the body .. But without the body coming apart, and it was not moved in pieces, but with complete lightness, as if it were the blink of an eye in which you are in one place and then are in another. This was an experience in a dream and not in reality.

My last advice before I conclude ..""")

t(30, 90, """The relationship with heaven .. The relationship with the Lord of heaven and the Lord of the whole universe, sanctified be His names .. Then with what He shows His servants if He wills; it is a relationship not built on asking for wonders and pursuing them .. Meaning you are not worshipping Allah .. You do that so that wonders happen to you .. Then you are not worshipping Allah .. Then Allah Most High does not matter to you and is not in your heart or your soul; you only have an aim and an interest, and your goal is not Allah Most High! What worship is this? The occurrence of wonders that break physics is a result you do not seek at all, do not think about, and that never crosses your mind when you truly worship Allah with real worship and are occupied with Him alone. So everyone who prayed for supernatural feats at the start of his commitment did not worship Allah. But asking for one of the supernatural feats is understandable when your relationship with Allah Most High has become excellent and there is a reason for asking, not merely to obtain them, and when, if you obtain them, you do not broadcast them or tell people about them, and they remain only between you and Allah Most High. This requires that your soul has moved to the world of the spirit, not that you are immersed in wronging people and in desires, pray 10 thousand rak'ahs a day and say “I want karamat” .. Then you want deception, not the witnessing of what steadies your heart so that you are helped, by the permission of the Most Merciful, on the hard and desolate road. For it truly is desolate and hard, and you may face a very great challenge on earth, as if the world were shut tight upon you, so you ask Allah Most High to break physics, not as a request for high rank but as the request of one in dire need, forced to it! And we do not believe any person who comes and says “I am transferred from place to place”, because this is a door of great trial for people; we block it at once before giving any chance at all for it to be opened, and we reject it from the root, completely and decisively .. This is the method.

In conclusion, we never, ever worship Allah Most High, sanctified be His names, so that He breaks something for us. It is enough for us to live worshipping Him, by His favour and grace upon us, with a good and well-guided worship to which He guides us as a grace from Him, and to die without any wonders or feats of physics; that does not matter. Because we do ((not)) worship Allah Most High for interests on earth, nor to tell and recount stories of what happened to us, nor to speak of details. We worship our Lord the Almighty only for Him, in Him and for His sake, and this is what should occupy us 24/24 hours, and nothing else.""")

t(30, 1090, """It set out from Ethiopia .. covered the west of Yemen, then bent toward the sea before reaching the east of Yemen and the Sultanate of Oman, then reached India and covered parts of it! This is a clear message .. to those who fear the punishments on earth and from heaven .. The message is: Allah Most High is the Owner of everything. He tells the wind: send the ash to that place and keep it away from that place .. Or He commands the volcanic ash itself, without any wind or any air, and tells it: keep away from that place and cover that place .. Many people (not all) think Allah Most High needs a wind to remove a danger, or needs something of the causes of His earth! When I lay on a hospital bed for 17 days in 2021, I saw Him, sanctified be His names .. I saw Him with my heart .. And I still, today in 2025 .. I still feel that very same dread .. The dread of the reality of His power .. His power which no mind can imagine .. His power, His greatness and the reality of His essence, sanctified be all His names and attributes .. Exalted .. and Mighty .. and Exalted .. and Mighty .. Sanctified above His heavens, His earth and His universes, whose number and nature no god but He knows .. Sanctified and Mighty above what He created, above what our minds conceive, and above what cannot be conceived at all .. When He wills a thing, it happens and comes to pass without a cause .. And when He wills a karamah for His righteous servants on His earth, He places a supplication in the hearts of those men and women, they utter it, and He answers them as an honour to them .. He wills what He wills .. does what He wills .. and chooses what He wills .. Magnify the Lord""")

t(31, 115, """If you are told the whole world has gone up in flames .. be with Allah the Almighty, our Lord .. Taking the means comes after, not before, taking refuge in Allah Most High .. Months ago I saw a dream of glad tidings for people .. I saw that I was in a ground-floor house, not my present house .. sitting on a prayer rug throughout the dream, praying and supplicating; then very strong explosions took place outside the house, which I saw while I was inside the house on the prayer rug, without going outside. So I prostrated to Allah the Almighty, our Lord, the Most Merciful, for a length of time in the dream; then I rose from prostration and the explosions had stopped. I actually went outside in the dream and found, in place of the fires and destruction, roses, crops and a gentle shining sun, and the people in the street happy and joyful, as if nothing had happened or occurred.""")

t(31, 1430, """The amount of weariness, pain, affliction, exhaustion, hardship and strain that you may pay from your blood, your soul, your spirit and everything, if you decide to hold fast to justice in your personal life and say: No .. I will not do wrong, is something your mind does not and will not imagine. It is an amount of mental and bodily pains and aches of which the least that can be said is that they are a painful torment, an abiding blaze and great agonies. Many people tire of paying the price at its start, so they back down and change their deeds from justice to injustice out of weariness at the beginning of the road, and relapse at its start .. Some fall and relapse in the middle of the road, having wasted every effort and toil that befell them.. And some stand firm by the might of Allah the Almighty, not by their own might or their own strength.

The scale of justice is the hardest .. the most difficult .. and the greatest cause of weariness and exhaustion in worldly life .. When the world .. and people .. and everything join together against you, and none has mercy on you but Allah .. and for long years people's mercy is stripped from your path, so they tear at you with their teeth and chew your flesh, your soul and your spirit without stopping .. When that happens to you because you were told: Do wrong .. and you said: I will not .. and the world attacked you like a raging wind .. then you are in the greatest test of all!""")

t(32, 490, """Tap on the pictures""")

t(32, 1575, """I receive questions about people who tell others that the first of the signs to appear is the sun rising from the west, and who cite a hadith that mentions this. The detail in this matter is very long, but in brief .. The following hadith is also authentic, in Sahih Muslim: The Prophet ﷺ said: “Hasten to do deeds before six things: the Dajjal, the smoke, the Beast of the earth, the rising of the sun from its west, the affair of the general public, and the private affair of each one of you” [Narrated by Muslim: 2947].

To avoid going on at length .. The rising of the sun from its west means the final closing of the door of repentance, and this fits with the emergence of the Beast that brands people as believer and disbeliever .. As for saying that the first of the signs is the rising of the sun from its west, that is a grave and great error in understanding, not in the wording of the hadith that says so .. Because the door of repentance will not be closed،،،، will not be closed،،،، ever .. as long as the tests on earth have not yet ended!
The Mahdi is a test and trial for Muslims and non-Muslims
The Great Battle is a test and trial for Muslims
The Dajjal is a test and trial for all mankind
Allah's prophet Jesus, peace be upon him, is a test for the Christians

Therefore, the sun will never, absolutely never, rise from its west as long as these tests have not yet ended

My words end here .. I am the servant in need of Allah Most High .. But whoever would like more, from the words of the scholars of the Salaf among the great scholars of the Ummah, here is the following:

Ibn Hajar said in al-Fath: What is preponderant from the reports taken together is that the emergence of the Dajjal is the first of the great signs announcing the change of general conditions over most of the earth, and that the rising of the sun from the west is the first of the great signs announcing the change of the conditions of the upper world; and perhaps the emergence of the Beast takes place on the same day on which the sun rises from the west... Al-Hakim said: What appears is that the rising of the sun precedes the emergence of the Beast, then the Beast emerges on that day or one close to it. End.

Al-Mubarakfuri said in his commentary on al-Tirmidhi: Know that the narrations differ on the order of the ten signs, and so the people of knowledge differed on their order. It has been said that the first of the signs is the smoke, then the emergence of the Dajjal, then the descent of Jesus, peace be upon him, then""")

t(33, 60, """the emergence of Gog and Magog, then the emergence of the Beast, then the rising of the sun from its west; for the disbelievers will accept Islam in the time of Jesus, peace be upon him, until the call is one, and had the sun risen from its west before the emergence of the Dajjal and his descent, faith would not have been accepted from the disbelievers. The “and” is for simple joining, so it is no objection that his descent is before its rising, nor is the report that the rising of the sun is the first of the signs... End.

As for the hadith of Muslim from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: I memorised from the Messenger of Allah that he said: “The first of the signs to appear are the rising of the sun from its west and the emergence of the Beast before the people in the forenoon; whichever of them comes before its companion, the other follows close on its heels.” The author of Awn al-Ma'bud said about it: Some have interpreted this hadith to mean that the signs are either indications of the nearness of the Hour or of its arrival; of the first kind are the Dajjal and the like, and of the second the rising of the sun and the like, so the rising of the sun is first only in relation to the second kind. End.

As for the hadith “Three, when they emerge”, it does not contradict what we mentioned about the emergence of the Dajjal being first, because the joining in the hadith is by “and”, which does not require order; with it the earlier may be joined to the later and the reverse.. As in the saying of the Most High: “He has ordained for you of religion what He enjoined on Noah, and that which We have revealed to you, and what We enjoined on Abraham, Moses and Jesus: Establish the religion and do not be divided in it. Hard for the polytheists is that to which you call them. Allah chooses for Himself whom He wills and guides to Himself whoever turns to Him” {Ash-Shura: 13}.""")

t(33, 860, """The brothers asking here in the comments about the volcanic cloud in the Sultanate of Oman .. Allah the Almighty, our Lord, has been gracious in decreeing that the cloud veer off to the Arabian Sea; it is over the sea heading toward the south of Pakistan and the north of India. In the Sultanate of Oman it did not arrive at all, praise be to Allah.""")

t(33, 1170, """Another, different world is coming, Allah willing""")

t(33, 2250, """O noble ones .. Hardly a day passes without my looking at pictures of the world and the cities 150 years ago .. I look at the people .. the streets.. People rushing to their work .. People practising their trades .. People eating.. People rejoicing .. getting married.. riding buses.. riding animals .. Each person living his reality .. his life .. his chance .. Then they died .. they all died .. This means that we too will die.. like them.. What does this mean? It means our story will end as their story ended! So what is it that people wrestle over? Wronging, hurting and not fearing their Lord? Everyone's stories will end.. as the earlier stories ended .. Then we will become a memory as they became a memory.. All of us will become a memory .. something that passed and went .. Those who live after us will say: So-and-so lived and died .. So-and-so lived and died .. They did not remember this end, except those who remembered .. Look at the picture of these dead! They had life projects .. They went out to work in the morning .. married.. had children .. celebrated.. bought and sold .. lived life to the full.. As if they would never die ..""")

t(34, 60, """as if they would never depart .. People today too (most of them) think their moment of departure will not come .. busy with the movement of life.. with its pulling them along .. Have they not heard it said: So-and-so died on his wedding night .. So-and-so fell ill suddenly and died .. So-and-so went suddenly and departed .. Not stopping is a mistake .. And rushing headlong is a mistake .. One must remember every day .. Remembering is salvation.. Remembering the Hereafter is wisdom .. intelligence .. discernment .. and the daily deed highest in rank with the Almighty Lord after worship""")

t(34, 1305, """Building a house in hours!""")

t(34, 2390, """For the attention of the brothers and sisters who follow the recitation broadcast on the channel: unfortunately, the broadcasting of further recitation will stop and we will make do with what is on the channel, because the state of exhaustion, fatigue and choking, and the visual effect on the vowel marks, have increased and become tiring and exhausting, steadily growing and not stopping at a set level .. Tonight's recitation was not recorded, and things were better, by the grace and favour of Allah Most High: no choking and no difficulty in reciting as happens when recording. We ask Allah Most High for blessing and benefit in what has been published .. and we ask Allah the Almighty, our Lord, for relief for us all, Allah willing.""")

t(35, 265, """Only hours before the Ethiopia volcano I wrote here: Divine punishments are of many kinds and are not confined to the sign of the smoke. Man narrows what is wide in the will of Allah .. The earth is full of volcanoes able to bring down empires, and of a sea that rages for seven days or for 7 minutes or for a fraction of a second by the power of Allah, which has nothing to do with physics, and takes everything in its path, and of a rain rained upon them that spares nothing and leaves nothing .. The Ethiopia volcano is a reminder to those who thought that the power of Allah is confined only to the sign of the smoke, and that He cannot destroy an oppressor except by one of the ten major signs, and cannot establish the truth on earth except by one of the ten major signs! The reply came: a volcano and a smoke from the earth and not from the sky.
As for our Lord's saying about the earth, when it takes on its adornment, that the command of Allah comes to it (“Our command comes to it”), ijtihad is open to reflecting that “Our command” is the sign of the smoke; but (“Our command”) has recurred many times in human history, and not once among those times was it the sign of the smoke! Because Allah the Almighty, our Lord, has sent down on the people of the earth various punishments over thousands of years, and not a single punishment among them was a major sign. So the major signs have been stored up for the decree of Allah Most High in the events of the end of the earth.

As for the ten major signs, they are not a mark of the end of great powers; Allah Most High brought down the mighty Roman Empire in its time with a mouse, not even with a volcano .. So the ten major signs, the smoke among them, are not for bringing down the great powers when they do wrong. Rather, the ten major signs are beads strung in order, one after another, with the quality of succession, to prepare the people of the earth for the Day of Resurrection. They are religious signs for the sake of religion, not for smashing great powers .. The smoke is for the sake of religion because it is tied to the Dajjal, Judaism, Christianity and Islam; the rising of the sun from the west is tied to religion because it is the closing of the door of repentance; the Beast relates to religion because it brands the believer and the disbeliever; the three sinkings of the earth relate to religion because through them the empowerment of the true religion begins; the fire that gathers people gathers them for the Day of Religion; the Dajjal emerges in an emergence that relates to religion; the descent of Allah's prophet Jesus is for the sake of religion; and Gog and Magog are a sign for ending wars on the face of the earth entirely for the sake of religion, so that Allah's prophet Jesus and the Muslims may enjoy practising their religion until the death of Allah's prophet Jesus without danger or wars, and so that religious wars end among mankind. Because Gog and Magog come out fighting for their atheistic creed, and atheism is one of the faces of belief; they say, that is, Gog and Magog, when they reach the Lake of Tiberias and find no one: We have killed the people of the earth, so let us kill the people of heaven, mocking and jeering. This shows that they are atheists; had they believed in the existence of a god they would not have said what they said. So their emergence is not political or military, but an emergence to kill every believing man and woman on earth. Hence their sign too is a major sign relating to religion and to their creed of atheism. It is magnifying a great power in the soul for a person to think it so mighty that our Lord the Almighty cannot bring it down except with a major sign; and this, by Allah, is""")

t(35, 1320, """a great failure to understand Allah Most High and His ways on earth, and part of the error of magnifying the powers of humans in the soul and deeming them very strong on the scale of the power of Allah the Almighty.

Our Lord the Almighty, sanctified be His names, says of the phrase “Our command came”, in a passage where there is none of the ten major signs:
“Until, when Our command came and the oven gushed forth, We said: Load upon it of every kind a pair, two, and your family, except him against whom the word has already gone forth, and whoever believes. But none believed with him except a few”""")

t(35, 1780, """Some brothers who write privately think I have abundant knowledge in one of the topics most discussed among Muslims today. Their questions are no crime and their interest in this topic is no mistake, but I am not the one fit to answer them on this matter .. I receive questions in private about Imam Mahdi .. I would like to say that this servant in need of Allah does not know the unseen; none knows the unseen but Allah Most High. And to show the reality of things, how there is no human on earth who encompasses everything, and how we toss about from one ignorance to another: I did not know what Imam Mahdi means, in his very simple basic details, except from my first wife. She is the one who acquainted me with the basic details that people know and I did not, and that was at the age of perhaps 23 .. So to the brothers who write to me, may Allah keep them: you are asking a person who, in his early youth, knew nothing of Imam Mahdi but his title. So do not count much on my possibly knowing a lot of information about him. Were it not for Allah's covering of us; and I reflect on Allah's covering and recall my ignorance in my early youth of the obvious things people know about the events of the end of time, and my 100% heedlessness of them, until I was taught by her whom Allah willed to teach me at that time .. So the Imam is hidden within the breasts and the understandings, and in that whose realities none know except those whom Allah has taught and for whom He willed that.""")

t(35, 2390, """And remind .. A note on WhatsApp that is hard for me to send to those who get in touch one by one .. one at a time, to those who got in touch and multiplied the titles .. And searching through the WhatsApp messages one by one is exhausting.

O noble ones .. I am not a sheikh, for sheikh means scholar, and I have not studied the sciences of the Shariah beyond some readings .. I am not an ustadh .. I am not a doctor, even though I hold higher degrees .. Even if a Muslim came to me one day and told me that a voice came to him""")

t(36, 60, """from heaven and said to him: tell Doctor Faraj such-and-such .. For heaven may send whatever it sends; that is an outpouring of the mercies, favour and generosity of the Almighty Lord .. But we here on earth are watched for what we do with what comes to us .. and how we act with what is opened to us .. There is no harm in an example being set .. We strive to make the model, and our reward is with Allah Most High .. Then I am not a sayyid either .. I am not, I am not

O noble ones .. Know that titles are like a throne in the heart, and it is not fitting for a human on earth to have a throne in his heart ..

Then this, which by Allah I hope for every believing man and woman and every Muslim man and woman: if every person were to meet Allah's prophet Muhammad and Allah's prophet Jesus, blessings and peace be upon them both, and Allah Most High unveiled to him in his vision their two beautiful hearts, he would realise that the greatest blessing after Islam is the blessing of understanding the truth .. Your brother passed through several different, varied and many stations of truth until I understood .. And when I understood, I was never again as I had been .. When I understood, I was thunderstruck by the truth of the truth .. and by the unveiling of the truth .. Then that was crowned with the model: two noble prophets of the resolute ones, their hearts more, and more, and more innocent than the heart of a child just born .. When I saw that with the eye of certainty .. and knew it with a knowledge that falsehood and doubt cannot approach from before it or behind it, and witnessed it with the witnessing of one against whom the proof of witnessing is established, who is not given it for amusement or comfort but to be held to account and punished .. When that happened to me I understood, I realised and I was freed .. I was freed from the illusions in which people are drowning .. and from the nonsense into which people have fallen .. and from the labels and titles in which people wander lost because they have adopted them .. So I am only brother Faraj, or only brother Omar, or Abu Muhammad .. or Faraj with nothing else, or Omar with nothing else .. All of that is true and right, and titles other than that are illusion, deception and a distancing from the truth .. The truth is what I saw in my heart of my two prophets Muhammad and Jesus, blessings and peace be upon them. That is the beautiful truth .. the truth that comforts the spirit .. the truth that, by Allah, is higher than a thousand thousand titles .. and than a thousand thousand professorships and doctorates .. the truth of the divine blessing .. the blessing of a person seeing himself as one of the people .. of them and with them .. For how many millions upon millions of ustadhs, doctors and professors are there? Millions and millions .. But Muhammad, may Allah bless him and his family and grant him peace, is only one person .. and Jesus, peace be upon him, is only one person .. and Moses, peace be upon him, is only one person .. I think the reader will now understand well what I saw in my heart of Allah's two noble prophets Muhammad and Jesus, blessings and peace be upon them .. and will understand that the truth is in their hearts, not in thrones set up inside hearts .. nor in titles by which the soul grows grand, swells and puffs up .. So I ask Allah Most High, for every believing man and woman, for our offspring, our neighbours, our wives and all believing spouses, the like of this that I am speaking about; and by Allah it is tremendous, but most people do not know.""")

t(36, 1345, """Please focus on what I am about to explain .. Unfortunately there is a great deal of wrong understanding among many people about a matter that is at the very core of mankind's coming future

The Prophet ﷺ said to Ibn Sayyad: “I have hidden something for you.” He said: “The dukh.” He said: “Away with you! You will never exceed your measure.” Omar said: “Permit me to strike his neck.” He said: “Leave him; if it is he, you will not be able to overpower him, and if it is not he, there is no good for you in killing him.”
Summary of the hadith scholar's ruling: [Authentic]
Narrator: Abdullah ibn Omar | Hadith scholar: al-Bukhari | Source: Sahih al-Bukhari

The Dajjal, the curse be upon him, in his dialogue with the Prophet ﷺ through the body of Ibn Sayyad, belittled the sign of the smoke. Why did he belittle it? Because the sign of the smoke does not affect his supernatural abilities .. Supernatural feats, not miracles .. Miracles are for prophets .. karamat are for the awliya .. and supernatural feats are for dajjals; even if he were a small dajjal in a village, what he brings with the help of the disbelieving jinn is supernatural feats.
The Dajjal has supernatural feats, so the sign of the smoke does not stop his feats. That is why he tried to make a diminutive of the word (dukhan) and said (dukh); so the Prophet ﷺ was angered, and al-Faruq, may Allah be pleased with him, who was present at the scene with the Prophet ﷺ, was angered at him.

So we have learned why the Dajjal does not see the sign of the smoke as a danger to him, and the answer is that he has supernatural feats. It is not true, as some of our brothers and sisters think, that he needs electricity because he will ride a plane .. and will make a hologram using electricity and broadcast it in the sky .. All of this is untrue .. When the Dajjal emerges in his clear, complete emergence, in which lie his death and annihilation, he will use the supernatural feats of the devils of the jinn; the door to that will be opened for him and he will be allowed it, so that the test on earth takes place .. But his anger at the sign of the smoke is not because it affects him directly, but because it affects the West, which has enjoyed the civilisation of electricity for centuries, and returns the world to before smart technology, that is, to the mechanical state, such as a pistol, gunpowder, rifles that work by the spark of gunpowder, and advanced bullets that are made even under the stairs in some areas of Pakistan and need no electricity to fill them with gunpowder; and the shift of weaponry from satellites to gunpowder alone, the firing of the remaining missiles on the battlefield of the Great Battle without electricity, and the equalling of military strength between the Muslims and the Romans, who have been defending his project for hundreds of years so that he is not forced to emerge in his complete emergence, which he never wants because he knows its end .. This is what will anger him, because the new victors will come very close to his place and he will turn into the heir of the defeat of a nation on which he has long relied .. Among them he will turn into one defeated, weak, wretched and broken, because their technological power, which will have ended, fallen and collapsed, was always the important psychological bond that tied them to him and made them loyal to him. So when the sign of the smoke comes and their civilisation ends entirely (almost), what of him is left for them to be loyal to him for? He will then see that the bond of interest between the Romans and him has fallen .. Only one thing will remain for him to stop the bleeding of his loss of the Romans, which is to emerge in his emergence, which has nothing to do with the laws of physics, nor electricity, nor reason, nor logic, from near or far, as many think .. The cause of the anger is that the relationship between him and the Romans will have collapsed, his small state in the Middle East collapsed, and all his effort of thousands of years gone to dust .. So the harm that will anger him is a harm""")
